  "min_tradable_equity_usd": 26.0,
  "_min_tradable_equity_usd_note": "Operator override of the derived floor. The derived value is what every enabled book needs to hold a position AT ONCE; below it the first book to fire consumes the budget and the rest sit margin-blocked, which looks from outside like books that do not fire (W-FUND1). $26.0 also acts as a drawdown brake: the system stops rather than grinding down.",
  "_xyz_concentration_note": "max_xyz_short_names 3 = max_concurrent, so the name cap never refuses a slot the concurrency budget already approved. It used to sit at 2 with max_concurrent 2 and produced 'REFUSED SHORT xyz:SNDK - xyz-short name cap reached (2/2)' while slots were free.\nmax_xyz_short_notional_pct 2.815 is the deployment expressed as notional: 92% of equity as margin x 3x = 2.76x equity, plus 2% slack. It is a PERCENT and has to be - it scales with the account, where a dollar cap would go stale in both directions.\nWhy it is not smaller: xyz shorts are ~1.28 effective bets at 0.83 mean pairwise correlation (W-MATH2/3; seven stopped together on 07-21 for -$8.59). The gate measures NOTIONAL and is right to - a correlated 15% move costs 15% of notional whatever the leverage. Sizing the book therefore means accepting a 41.4% correlated drawdown, which is why that number is declared explicitly in max_correlated_drawdown_pct rather than left implied.",
  "max_correlated_drawdown_pct": 0.1817,
